<title>UK: UK's Brown sees EU agreement with jobs at heart.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown sees EU agreement with jobs at heart.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said on Monday that an agreement over the European Union's stability pact was close to being achieved with jobs at the heart of the accord.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we're getting to an agreement about these four things,&quot; Brown told BBC radio. &quot;Firstly, jobs are absolutely central, secondly you've got to look at new ways of creating jobs and thirdly that job creation is not inconsistent with stability.</p>
<p>&quot;Finally, of course, if stability is important, you can't fudge criteria if you're talking about monetary union.&quot;</p>
</text>
